<title>BRAZIL: BRAZIL'S SENATE APPROVES FRANCO AS CENBANK HEAD.</title>
<headline>BRAZIL'S SENATE APPROVES FRANCO AS CENBANK HEAD.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Senate has approved the nomination of Gustavo Franco as the new president of the country's Central Bank, an official said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Senate president Sen. Antonio Carlos Magalhaes said 56 members of the upper house voted in favor of Franco's nomination and 10 voted against.  </p>
<p>The vote was the last hurdle in the way of Franco's promotion to the top job in the Central Bank, where he is currently international affairs director.</p>
<p>(( --Michael Christie, Brasilia newsroom 5561 3141193))</p>
